{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: verbatim duplication of the start-error card**

The new `bootError` branch is a character-for-character copy of the `_startError` branch directly above (`Padding(24)` + `Text(appsStartError(...))` + error color styling) — ~15 duplicated lines that will drift (one gets a retry button, the other doesn't — which is already the case between this card and the canvas's `_errorTile`). Extract a local helper:

```dart
Widget _errorCard(ThemeData theme, Object error) => Center(
      child: Padding(
        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(24),
        child: Text(
          context.l10n.appsStartError('$error', widget.app.name),
          textAlign: TextAlign.center,
          style: theme.textTheme.bodyMedium?.copyWith(
            color: theme.colorScheme.error,
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );
```

Then `_startError` and `bootError` branches each become one line. (The board tile side already shares its fallback — both `_startError` and `bootError` render the same `AppIcon` — so only the view needs this.)
